ou’ll be able to type it in directly by creating a new entry in your database (usually called a library by the softwar
e). Typing the information yourself is the most time-consuming method, but also sometimes the most reliable, as other me
thods rely on data being transferred from one computer system to another. These automated methods can sometimes introduc
e errors in interpretation, for example when one system outputs data in a format that doesn’t match what the other sys
tem expects. When you enter it by yourself, field by field, you can be sure that all of the relevant information is capt
ured (as long as you don’t make any typos…). You’ll probably also be able to import the referencing information by
