rk you carried out. You might have a section for lab methodologies and another for fieldwork methodologies (this means y
ou can group individual methods in a logical, sequential order, thus helping your reader follow your processes more easi
ly). Each of the methods (the individual processes) might be adapted from literature you’ve read. Grouping those liter
ature references in your database on the basis of these two broad methodology sections would make your life easier when 
browsing your library and deciding which articles you need to use as references in your thesis. The alternative would be
 to read through the titles and abstracts in your reference manager one-by-one until you identified all the articles you
